.TH VALLUM 8 "2026-10-19" "vallum 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
vallum \- hybrid post-quantum layer-3 tunnel
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vallum
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vallum
runs a layer-3 tunnel with a tri-hybrid KEM handshake and an explicit,
mutually authenticated key confirmation. It is configured by a TOML file; the
daemon owns the tunnel, the TUN interface and the UDP socket, and nothing else.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run --config FILE
Run the tunnel. Requires CAP_NET_ADMIN for the interface and socket.
.TP
.B keygen --output FILE [--suite ID] [--signing]
Generate a private key and print the peer public line.
.TP
.B pubkey --private-key FILE
Print the public line for an existing key.
.TP
.B genpsk
Print a fresh 32-byte preshared key as 64 hex characters.
.TP
.B show [--config FILE | --control SOCKET] [--dump] [--json] [--watch] [--field NAME]
Query a running daemon's control socket. `--json` is secret-free; `--watch`
refreshes until Ctrl-C.
.TP
.B setconf FILE
Replace every peer with the config's peers.
.TP
.B addconf FILE
Add or update the config's peers.
.TP
.B syncconf FILE
Apply only the differences, preserving unchanged sessions.
.TP
.B showconf [--config FILE | --control SOCKET] [--include-secrets]
Export a config; secrets are omitted unless explicitly requested.
.TP
.B bench [--suite ID] [--bytes N] [--iterations N]
Measure the data plane's seal/open cost.
.TP
.B doctor [--config FILE | --control SOCKET] [--json]
Check the platform, config, control socket, and helper tools.
.TP
.B completions SHELL
Print a completion script for bash, zsh, fish, or PowerShell.
.TP
.B tui [--config FILE | --control SOCKET | --config-dir DIR] [--snapshot]
Open the terminal operations console. `--snapshot` renders one frame headlessly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/vallum/*.toml
Configuration files.
.TP
.I /run/vallum/*.sock
Control sockets, mode 0600.
.SH SECURITY
The private key is refused if its file is group- or world-readable, unless
.B --allow-insecure-key-permissions
is given. The control socket is same-user only. The daemon runs no shell and
writes no routes; use
.BR vallum-quick (8)
for host-level work. The TUI spawns `systemctl`, `journalctl`, `vallum-quick`,
and `$EDITOR` with argument arrays; it does not open a shell.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vallum-quick (8),
.BR vallum.toml (5)
